# Additions to Alpine's dnsmasq profile (apparmor-profiles), which only
# expects libvirt to manage dnsmasq. NetworkManager runs it as the local
# DNS server (dns=dnsmasq): it reads dnsmasq's /proc entries to check its
# pid file and stops it with a signal.

# Signals from root's shells and what they run (kill, rc-service, ...),
# which Alpine's busybox profile, in unconfined mode, labels busybox
signal (receive) peer=busybox,

signal (receive) peer=NetworkManager,
ptrace (readby) peer=NetworkManager,
